From 28e6b8244c21a7d6ee884f4d470efa3c3faf7cec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2025 16:50:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] i2c: i2c-qcom-geni: Fix NULL pointer dereference issue
 for CCU QUP

During CCU mode selection, the driver dereferences a channel without
verifying its presence, leading to NULL pointer dereference.

To resolve this issue, Add check to ensure the channel exists before
accessing it. Additionally, the logic has been optimized to allocate
all channels during the probe phase, thereby eliminating the need to
select GPI DMA mode during each channel allocation.

[   72.598764][ T2753] Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000000001b8
[   72.598914][ T2753] Call trace:
[   72.598915][ T2753]  ccu_gpi_configure_mode+0x14/0x108 [gpi]
[   72.598919][ T2753]  geni_i2c_configure_ccu_mode+0x88/0x178 [i2c_qcom_geni]
[   72.598923][ T2753]  ccu_configure_mode+0x54/0xe8
[   72.598931][ T2753]  ccu_config_write+0x19c/0x458.

Change-Id: I8c7178647cd052f29fff29a02ce18a63b4c573f6
Signed-off-by: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
